    <DataNode elementId="AT3G06510-MONOMER" textLabel="Galactolipid galactosyltransferase SFR2, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q93Y07" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="735" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="zhang, THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, pmngroup">galactolipid:galactolipid galactosyltransferase (GGGT) activity, which is not detectable under normal growth conditions, was detected in the Arabidopsis tgd1 mutant. Under certain circumstances, plants can synthesize higher galactosylated forms of galactoglycerolipids. UDP-galactose is not the galactosyl donor. The galactosyl linkages are all in beta form.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G06510-MONOMER" />
